# What not to send to the Docker daemon as build context.
#
# This is deliberately NOT a copy of .gitignore, for two reasons that would
# each cause a quiet failure:
#
#   1. Docker patterns are anchored to the context root; git's match at any
#      depth. `*.out` here means only a *.out beside this file, so every
#      pattern below that should match anywhere carries an explicit `**/`.
#
#   2. .gitignore excludes `testdata/fuzz/`, and this file deliberately does
#      NOT. One fuzz seed is tracked — internal/pdf/testdata/fuzz/FuzzPDF/
#      fc7a8f950c971d7f, force-added past that rule — and a corpus entry the
#      fuzzer finds locally would land in that same directory. No pattern can
#      tell the two apart, so excluding the directory would cost internal/pdf
#      its seed. A few kilobytes of build context is the cheaper mistake.
#
# What must NOT be excluded, because the root module's tests read the working
# tree by relative path:
#
#   docs/          explain_golden_test.go reads docs/explainability.md and
#                  FAILS rather than skips when it is missing;
#                  defaults_doc_test.go parses docs/confidence.md
#   api/           api_test.go reads api/ovrin.txt
#   eval/corpus/   extract_test.go and render/pdfium's benchmarks read it
#   testdata/      the root PDF fixtures
#
# A lean "source only" ignore file turns several tests red and several others
# into silent skips, which is worse.

# The big one: 39MB of a 54MB tree, against ~5MB of tracked content.
.git
.gitattributes

# Local build and test output.
**/receipt
!examples/receipt/receipt.png
.bin/
bin/
dist/
**/*.exe
**/*.dll
**/*.so
**/*.dylib
**/*.test
**/*.out
**/coverage.*

# Evaluation output is generated, and the local variants are gitignored.
eval/report/*.local.*

# The Go workspace is local to each contributor and points outside this
# repository. The image sets GOWORK=off, but not copying it in the first place
# means there is nothing to ignore.
go.work
go.work.sum

# Editors and OS noise.
.vscode/
.idea/
**/*.swp
**/*~
**/.DS_Store

# Credentials never enter an image.
.env
.env.*

# Docker's own files are not needed inside the image.
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
docker-compose.yml

# Note the absence of a testdata/fuzz rule here — see point 2 at the top.
